@@ -75,6 +77,41 @@ This will end the request with `400 - Bad Request` status code and the following
 > [!IMPORTANT]
 > Error `statusText` should be short (max 512 to 1024 characters) and only include tab, spaces or visible ASCII characters and extended characters (byte value 128–255). Prefer `message` in JSON body for extended message.
 
+## Problem Details
+
+Set `problemDetails: true` to render errors as [RFC 9457](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457) `application/problem+json`:
+
+```js
+const app = new H3({ problemDetails: true });
+
+app.get("/", () => {
+  throw new HTTPError({
+    status: 403,
+    message: "Not allowed",
+    type: "https://example.com/errors/forbidden",
+    instance: "/orders/42",
+  });
+});
+```
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "https://example.com/errors/forbidden",
+  "title": "Forbidden",
+  "status": 403,
+  "detail": "Not allowed",
+  "instance": "/orders/42"
+}
+```
+
+- `title` is the error `statusText` or a standard phrase for common statuses (omitted otherwise).
+- `detail` is the error `message` (omitted when it only repeats `title`).
+- `type` and `instance` should be URIs. They are omitted when not set.
+- `data` is kept under the `data` key and `body` properties are added at the top level (they cannot override `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail` or `instance`).
+- [Unhandled errors](#unhandled-errors) only expose `title` and `status` (plus `stack` with `debug`).
+
+Errors rendered outside the app (for example `handler.fetch` of a standalone handler) keep the default JSON format.
+
 ## Unhandled Errors
 
 Any error that occurs during calling [request lifecycle](/guide/basics/lifecycle) without using `HTTPError` will be processed as an _unhandled_ error.
